      "feedback": "Yes — base 2: 2^(2x) = 2³ gives 2x = 3, so x = 3/2."
     },
     {
      "id": "b",
      "label": "2",
      "feedback": "4² = 16, too big. Rewriting base 2 gives x = 3/2."
     },
     {
      "id": "c",
      "label": "1/2",
      "feedback": "4^(1/2) = 2, too small. The answer is x = 3/2."
     }
    ]
   },
   "variant": {
    "gen": "a1-exponential",
    "form": "exp-match-base__mcq"
   }
  },
